---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config.js';
---

<Page
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  eyebrow="About"
  lede="An independent reference for documented organizations, people, places and institutions."
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} publishes source-backed profiles of real-world entities: schools, universities, people,
    organizations and places. Each profile gathers what the public record actually contains about a subject —
    government records, awarding-body documentation, press reporting and the subject's own statements — and
    attributes every claim to the source it came from.
  </p>

  <h2>Why the site exists</h2>
  <p>
    Information about many real-world entities is fragmented. A school's award sits in a PDF on one site, its
    government registration in a spreadsheet on another, and its public activity in a decade of local newspaper
    archives. Nobody has assembled it, so a reader searching the entity's name finds directory listings that
    reproduce each other's unverified data.
  </p>
  <p>
    A profile here does that assembly, and shows its working. That means saying plainly which claims rest on
    independent reporting, which come from the subject itself, and which could not be verified at all.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not copy content from encyclopedias or reproduce deleted articles from elsewhere.</li>
    <li>We do not publish claims we could not trace to a source we have read.</li>
    <li>We do not accept payment to create, alter, favourably frame or remove a profile.</li>
    <li>We do not describe a subject as "best", "top" or "leading" without independent evidence.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/about/methodology/">Methodology</a> — how a profile is researched and built.</li>
    <li><a href="/about/source-policy/">Source policy</a> — what we cite and what we refuse to cite.</li>
    <li><a href="/about/editorial-policy/">Editorial policy</a> — neutrality, independence and review.</li>
    <li><a href="/about/corrections/">Corrections</a> — how to get something fixed.</li>
    <li><a href="/about/muhammad-abdullah-al-yasin/">Who writes this</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial and general enquiries: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    Corrections: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.correctionsEmail}`}>{SITE.correctionsEmail}</a>, or use the
    <a href="/contact/"> contact form</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
